aces by ID, as a JSON array."},"1335":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-103","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#lookup","content":"osm_ids · yes · Comma-separated teigeodata IDs, at most 50; an OSM reference such as N123 is left out as not found.","table":"table-17"},"1336":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-104","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#lookup","content":"addressdetails · 1: add each place's address.","table":"table-17"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-105","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#lookup","content":"format · json (the default), jsonv2 (the same) or geojson.","table":"table-17"},"1338":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-106","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#lookup","content":"json_callback · Refused: JSONP is not supported.","table":"table-17"},"1339":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-107","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#other-routes","content":"/packs · The packs served: each one's release, components, places and attribution.","table":"table-18"},"1340":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-108","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#other-routes","content":"/health · {\"status\": \"ok\", \"layers\": n} while the server answers.","table":"table-18"},"1341":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-109","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#other-routes","content":"/mcp · The MCP server, over Streamable HTTP.","table":"table-18"},"1342":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-110","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"A failure answers `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}` with the code's HTTP status; a Nominatim route puts the status in `code`. Codes are stable: one may be added, none changes its meaning."},"1343":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-111","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"invalid_argument · 400 · A parameter does not parse or has no meaning (a bad ID, a latitude past 90°).","table":"table-19"},"1344":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-112","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"out_of_bounds · 400 · A parameter is past a server bound: too long a text, too large a limit, too far a radius. A query string that is too long answers 414.","table":"table-19"},"1345":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-113","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"not_found · 404 · The place is not in the packs, or there is no such route.","table":"table-19"},"1346":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-114","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"missing_component · 501 · The packs served lack the component that answers this.","table":"table-19"},"1347":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-115","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"unauthenticated · 401 · The caller must say who they are: only a deployment that adds keys answers it.","table":"table-19"},"1348":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-116","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"forbidden · 403 · The caller may not ask this: only a deployment that adds rules answers it.","table":"table-19"},"1349":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-117","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"rate_limited · 429 · Too much, too fast: only a deployment that adds limits answers it.","table":"table-19"},"1350":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-118","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"unavailable · 503 · The server cannot answer now (the request took longer than its timeout); asking again later may work.","table":"table-19"},"1351":{"id":"/docs/reference/http-119","page_id":"/docs/reference/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/http#errors","content":"internal · 500 · The server failed; never the client's fault.","table":"table-19"},"1352":{"id":"/docs/reference","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"page","content":"Reference","breadcrumbs":["teigeodata","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference"},"1353":{"id":"/docs/reference-0","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"Every function, method, record and error of the API, with its documentation and its declaration in each language."},"1354":{"id":"/docs/reference-1","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"Engine"},"1355":{"id":"/docs/reference-2","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"Store"},"1356":{"id":"/docs/reference-3","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"Job"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/reference-4","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"Functions"},"1358":{"id":"/docs/reference-5","page_id":"/docs/reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference#types-constants-and-errors","content":"Types, constants and errors"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/reference-6","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"The API is defined once, in Rust (`teigeodata-api`), and every binding is generated from that\ndefinition, so this reference is generated from it too: each entry gives the documentation\nwritten in the API and the declaration each language's binding is written with. It holds\n33 engine methods, 22\nstore and job methods and 8 functions."},"1360":{"id":"/docs/reference-7","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"Names follow each language's style; the entries use the Rust ones:"},"1361":{"id":"/docs/reference-8","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"search_with · searchWith · SearchWith · tg_engine_search_with","table":"table-0"},"1362":{"id":"/docs/reference-9","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"admin_at · adminAt · AdminAt · tg_engine_admin_at","table":"table-0"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/reference-10","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"tz_offset_at · tzOffsetAt · TzOffsetAt · tg_engine_tz_offset_at","table":"table-0"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/reference-11","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference","content":"Queries return a result blob read with each language's `Reader`.\nThe servers have their own reference: every route of the HTTP API\nand every tool of the MCP server, generated from the servers' own\ndefinitions."},"1365":{"id":"/docs/reference-12","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"The Engine page has each method's declaration in every language."},"1366":{"id":"/docs/reference-13","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"new · An engine with no packs.","table":"table-1"},"1367":{"id":"/docs/reference-14","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_file · Opens the pack at path (memory-mapped) and adds it.","table":"table-1"},"1368":{"id":"/docs/reference-15","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_file_with · Opens the pack at path with these options and adds it.","table":"table-1"},"1369":{"id":"/docs/reference-16","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_file_range · Opens the pack stored whole in length bytes at offset of the file at path (memory-mapped) and adds it: a pack bundled as an uncompressed asset of an Android app (noCompress; the path is the APK, the offset and length its AssetFileDescriptor's), or one inside any container that stores it uncompressed.","table":"table-1"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/reference-17","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_file_range_with · As open_file_range, with these options.","table":"table-1"},"1371":{"id":"/docs/reference-18","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_bytes · Adds a pack from its bytes (copied).","table":"table-1"},"1372":{"id":"/docs/reference-19","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"open_bytes_with · Adds a pack from its bytes (copied) with these options.","table":"table-1"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/reference-20","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"remove · Removes the pack with this layer ID; false if no pack has it.","table":"table-1"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/reference-21","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"layers · The number of packs.","table":"table-1"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/reference-22","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"get · The place with this ID (tgd:np/1), or no row; a retired ID gives its survivor.","table":"table-1"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/reference-23","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"parent · The place's parent as the packs answer for it (one row), or no row for a root or an unknown ID.","table":"table-1"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/reference-24","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"ancestors · The place's ancestors, parent first up to the country; no rows for a root or an unknown ID.","table":"table-1"},"1378":{"id":"/docs/reference-25","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"children · The place's children, by ID; no rows for a leaf or an unknown ID.","table":"table-1"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/reference-26","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"nearby · The places nearest the place with this ID, not counting it, nearest first, at most limit, with meters and bearing (from each place to it); no rows for an unknown ID.","table":"table-1"},"1380":{"id":"/docs/reference-27","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"search · Places matching query, best first, at most limit; \"Name, Parent\" ranks a named parent first.","table":"table-1"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/reference-28","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"search_with · search ranked by options: near a focus point, or in strict match order.","table":"table-1"},"1382":{"id":"/docs/reference-29","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"reverse · The places nearest the point, nearest first, at most limit, with meters and bearing (degrees clockwise from north, from each place to the point).","table":"table-1"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/reference-30","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"within_radius · The places within radius_m metres of the point (great-circle), nearest first, at most limit, with meters and bearing (from each place to the point).","table":"table-1"},"1384":{"id":"/docs/reference-31","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"admin_at · The admin units holding the point, country first.","table":"table-1"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/reference-32","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"elevation_at · The terrain height at the point, as one row: meters above the datum (bilinear between the DEM samples around it), source (the DEM product's key, null where the pack does not state it), resolution_m (the sample spacing north to south) and datum (EGM2008).","table":"table-1"},"1386":{"id":"/docs/reference-33","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"postal_lookup · The places postal code code names, one row per code and place, with the code's postal, scheme, code_kind, valid_from and valid_to columns.","table":"table-1"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/reference-34","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"postal_prefix · Up to limit postal codes starting with prefix, with their places (autocomplete), in code order per scheme; scheme as in postal_lookup.","table":"table-1"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/reference-35","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"postal_codes_of · The postal codes of the place with this ID; no rows for an unknown ID.","table":"table-1"},"1389":{"id":"/docs/reference-36","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"postal_at · The postal codes of the point: those of the deepest admin unit holding it that an admin-aligned scheme gives codes to, with its parts (a ward's code; the point is in one of them).","table":"table-1"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/reference-37","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_at · The time-zone area holding the point (one row; its tz column is the IANA zone), or no row where no pack answers.","table":"table-1"},"1391":{"id":"/docs/reference-38","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_offset_at · The UTC offset in force in zone (a tzdb name or link, Asia/Kathmandu) at unix_seconds, from the first layer whose zone rules hold the zone: one row with seconds east of UTC, dst (1 when tzdb counts it as daylight saving time) and abbr (+0545, EDT); no row where no layer holds the zone.","table":"table-1"},"1392":{"id":"/docs/reference-39","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_local · The offsets a civil time may have in zone: one row with kind (unique, gap for a time a transition skips, overlap for one that happens twice), before and after in seconds east of UTC (the offsets before and after the transition: for an overlap the earlier and the later instant's; for a unique time both the same); no row where no layer holds the zone.","table":"table-1"},"1393":{"id":"/docs/reference-40","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_zones · Every zone name (tzdb names and links) the layers' zone rules hold, in byte order: one zone column.","table":"table-1"},"1394":{"id":"/docs/reference-41","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_rules_start · The earliest instant zone's rules cover, in Unix seconds: one unix row (its first transition, before which tzdb knows only local mean time; the year −9,999 for a zone that never changed); no row where no layer holds the zone.","table":"table-1"},"1395":{"id":"/docs/reference-42","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"tz_version · The tzdb release (2026f) of the first layer with zone rules; empty without rules.","table":"table-1"},"1396":{"id":"/docs/reference-43","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"by_iso · The place whose ISO 3166 code is code (NP, NP-P3, either case), or no row.","table":"table-1"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/reference-44","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"boundary · The outline of the place with this ID at level of detail lod, as one row: id, lod (the level read: 0 from a pack stored at full resolution only), tolerance_m (how far it may stray from the full-resolution outline), vertices and geojson, an RFC 7946 Feature ready for a map: a Polygon or MultiPolygon (outer rings counterclockwise, holes clockwise), or the place's Point when it has no outline.","table":"table-1"},"1398":{"id":"/docs/reference-45","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#engine","content":"distance · The great-circle distance between the places with these IDs, as one row: meters on the mean Earth sphere and bearing, the initial bearing from from to to in degrees clockwise from north.","table":"table-1"},"1399":{"id":"/docs/reference-46","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"The Store page has each method's declaration in every language."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/reference-47","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"create · Sets up a store at root and opens it: the metadata mirrors repo and asset mirrors assets (comma-separated URLs), and trusted_root, the catalog's root metadata, which becomes its trust anchor once it verifies by itself.","table":"table-2"},"1401":{"id":"/docs/reference-48","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"open · Opens the store at root, finishing or undoing an install a crash cut short.","table":"table-2"},"1402":{"id":"/docs/reference-49","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"damaged · The packs found damaged when the store was opened, comma-separated; empty when none.","table":"table-2"},"1403":{"id":"/docs/reference-50","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"catalog · The verified catalog as stored, one row per pack, with its state against the store.","table":"table-2"},"1404":{"id":"/docs/reference-51","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"status · Each installed pack and its health, from a full check of every byte when deep.","table":"table-2"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/reference-52","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"pin · Pins the pack (kept when room is made), or unpins it.","table":"table-2"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/reference-53","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"remove · Removes the packs and the dependencies nothing else needs; returns what was removed.","table":"table-2"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/reference-54","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"find · The places named query in engine (one over a world pack the app ships, the installed packs, or both), best first, each with the catalog's packs that cover it: what to install for \"Dubai\".","table":"table-2"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/reference-55","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"locate · The countries within radius_m metres of a point in engine, each with the catalog's packs that cover the point: what to install for where the user stands.","table":"table-2"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/reference-56","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"engine · An engine over the installed packs, each opened with the components and languages installed.","table":"table-2"},"1410":{"id":"/docs/reference-57","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"refresh · Refreshes the catalog for the countries (comma-separated ISO codes) and every country installed.","table":"table-2"},"1411":{"id":"/docs/reference-58","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"install · Installs the packs with options, dependencies first, refreshing the catalog for their countries.","table":"table-2"},"1412":{"id":"/docs/reference-59","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"install_pass · One pass of an install whose bytes a platform's own download service fetches, for downloads that must go on while the app is suspended.","table":"table-2"},"1413":{"id":"/docs/reference-60","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"update · Updates the packs (every installed one when empty) to the catalog's releases, keeping the components and languages installed.","table":"table-2"},"1414":{"id":"/docs/reference-61","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#store","content":"repair · Checks the pack in full and, unless it is whole, fetches what it lacks.","table":"table-2"},"1415":{"id":"/docs/reference-62","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"A job's methods are on the Store page."},"1416":{"id":"/docs/reference-63","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"wait_progress · Waits until the progress moves past seq (from seq), the job ends, or timeout_ms passes; returns the sequence then.","table":"table-3"},"1417":{"id":"/docs/reference-64","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"seq · The progress's sequence number: it moves on with every change.","table":"table-3"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/reference-65","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"done_bytes · Bytes received so far.","table":"table-3"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/reference-66","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"total_bytes · Bytes expected, from the catalog's sizes: never below the bytes received, and equal to them once the job ends.","table":"table-3"},"1420":{"id":"/docs/reference-67","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"is_ended · Whether the job has ended (done, failed or cancelled); its result is then ready.","table":"table-3"},"1421":{"id":"/docs/reference-68","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"cancel · Asks the job to stop at its next request or chunk; it then fails with ErrorCode::Cancelled and leaves the store as it was.","table":"table-3"},"1422":{"id":"/docs/reference-69","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#job","content":"result · The job's result, waiting for it to end.","table":"table-3"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/reference-70","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"The functions page has each declaration in every language."},"1424":{"id":"/docs/reference-71","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"version · The library version, from its package metadata.","table":"table-4"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/reference-72","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"components · The components this build answers, in table order, comma-separated (point, elevation, admin).","table":"table-4"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/reference-73","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"noop · Does nothing.","table":"table-4"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/reference-74","page_id":"/docs/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference#functions","content":"fold · The search fold of a name: NFKD, lower case, optional accents dropped by script, spaces collapsed, recomposed to NFC.","table":"table-4"},"1428":{"id":"/doc