t (`np`, `np.dem`), several comma-separated. Results are blobs:"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"`catalog`: `path`, `release`, `download`, `disk`, `components`, `licence`, `state` (`available`, `installed` or `update`);"},"1730":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"`status`: `path`, `release`, `bytes`, `pinned`, `asked`, `health` (`good`, `length`, `head`, `footer` or `sections`), `components`;"},"1731":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"an install or update: `path`, `release`, `fetched`, `reused`, `kept`, `changed`;"},"1732":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"a refresh: `timestamp`, `files`, `bytes`; a repair: `path`, `health`, `fetched`; `remove`: `path`, `release`;"},"1733":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"`find` and `locate`: one row per place and pack that covers it: `id`, `name`, `lat`, `lon`, `countries`, then the pack's `pack`, `release`, `download`, `disk` and `state`, null for a place no pack in the catalog covers."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-33","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"Sets up a store at `root` and opens it: the metadata mirrors `repo` and asset mirrors `assets` (comma-separated URLs), and `trusted_root`, the catalog's root metadata, which becomes its trust anchor once it verifies by itself. A store set up before is set up again with these."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if the root does not verify or the store cannot be written."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#open","content":"Opens the store at `root`, finishing or undoing an install a crash cut short."},"1738":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-37","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#open","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if it is not a store or its journal cannot be read."},"1739":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-38","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#open","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-39","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#damaged","content":"The packs found damaged when the store was opened, comma-separated; empty when none. `repair` fetches what they lack."},"1741":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-40","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#catalog","content":"The verified catalog as stored, one row per pack, with its state against the store."},"1742":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-41","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#catalog","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` before a refresh, or if the stored catalog no longer verifies."},"1743":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-42","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#catalog","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1744":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-43","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#status","content":"Each installed pack and its health, from a full check of every byte when `deep`."},"1745":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-44","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#status","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if a pack cannot be read."},"1746":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-45","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#status","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1747":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-46","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#pin","content":"Pins the pack (kept when room is made), or unpins it."},"1748":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-47","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#pin","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if it is not installed."},"1749":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-48","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#pin","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1750":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-49","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#remove","content":"Removes the packs and the dependencies nothing else needs; returns what was removed."},"1751":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-50","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#remove","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if one is not installed or another pack needs it."},"1752":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-51","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#remove","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1753":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-52","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#find","content":"The places named `query` in `engine` (one over a world pack the app ships, the installed packs, or both), best first, each with the catalog's packs that cover it: what to install for \"Dubai\". Runs offline on the stored catalog."},"1754":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-53","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#find","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` for a limit above `LIMIT_MAX`; `ErrorCode::Refused` if the stored catalog no longer verifies."},"1755":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-54","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#find","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1756":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-55","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#locate","content":"The countries within `radius_m` metres of a point in `engine`, each with the catalog's packs that cover the point: what to install for where the user stands."},"1757":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-56","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#locate","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` for a point off the globe; `ErrorCode::Refused` if the stored catalog no longer verifies."},"1758":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-57","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#locate","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1759":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-58","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#engine","content":"An engine over the installed packs, each opened with the components and languages installed."},"1760":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-59","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#engine","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Io` or `ErrorCode::Corrupt` if a pack cannot be opened."},"1761":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-60","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#engine","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-61","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#refresh","content":"Refreshes the catalog for the countries (comma-separated ISO codes) and every country installed. Fails with `ErrorCode::Network` or `ErrorCode::Refused`."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-62","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install","content":"Installs the packs with `options`, dependencies first, refreshing the catalog for their countries. Cancelled, it leaves the store as it was; the packs installed before the one cut stay installed."},"1764":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-63","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` for an unknown component or language tag, more than 8 languages, or an outline level above 255; the job's own errors are the job's."},"1765":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-64","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install_pass","content":"One pass of an install whose bytes a platform's own download service fetches, for downloads that must go on while the app is suspended. The pass reads each asset's ranges from files under `dir`, checks every byte as from any host, and its result lists what is still missing, one row per range: `pack`, `urls` (the asset on each mirror, one per line), `length` (the asset's), `start` and `end` (the range, end exclusive) and `file`, where to save those bytes. Fetch every listed range (an HTTP `Range` request for `bytes=start-(end-1)`), then run the pass again; a result with no rows means the packs are installed and their files under `dir` removed. A first install takes three passes."},"1766":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-65","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install_pass","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` as for `Store::install`, or for an empty `dir`; the job's own errors are the job's."},"1767":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-66","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#update","content":"Updates the packs (every installed one when empty) to the catalog's releases, keeping the components and languages installed."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-67","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#repair","content":"Checks the pack in full and, unless it is whole, fetches what it lacks."},"1769":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-68","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#job","content":"A store's long work on a thread of its own: its progress in bytes, a wait for the next change, a cancel, and its result."},"1770":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-69","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#job","content":"**Job.** Each language builds its own idioms on these methods: a stream of progress, and the awaited result cancelling the job when the caller's task is cancelled."},"1771":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-70","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#wait_progress","content":"Waits until the progress moves past `seq` (from `seq`), the job ends, or `timeout_ms` passes; returns the sequence then. Polling with the last one returned sees every change."},"1772":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-71","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#wait_progress","content":"**Blocks.** Until the job moves or ends: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1773":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-72","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#seq","content":"The progress's sequence number: it moves on with every change."},"1774":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-73","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#done_bytes","content":"Bytes received so far."},"1775":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-74","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#total_bytes","content":"Bytes expected, from the catalog's sizes: never below the bytes received, and equal to them once the job ends."},"1776":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-75","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#is_ended","content":"Whether the job has ended (done, failed or cancelled); its result is then ready."},"1777":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-76","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#cancel","content":"Asks the job to stop at its next request or chunk; it then fails with `ErrorCode::Cancelled` and leaves the store as it was."},"1778":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-77","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#result","content":"The job's result, waiting for it to end."},"1779":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-78","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#result","content":"**Errors.** The job's: `ErrorCode::Network`, `ErrorCode::Refused`, `ErrorCode::Cancelled`, or `ErrorCode::Io` and `ErrorCode::Corrupt` for an engine's packs."},"1780":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-79","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#result","content":"**Blocks.** Until the job moves or ends: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1781":{"id":"/docs/reference/types","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"page","content":"Types, constants and errors","breadcrumbs":["teigeodata","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/types","content":"The options records, their enums, the limits and every error code, as each language names them."},"1783":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#options-records","content":"Options records"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#searchoptions","content":"`SearchOptions`"},"1785":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#openoptions","content":"`OpenOptions`"},"1786":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#installoptions","content":"`InstallOptions`"},"1787":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#enums","content":"Enums"},"1788":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/types#verify","content":"`Verify`"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/reference/types-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/types","type":"head